      "content": "That feeling of emptiness, like a hollow shell, is profoundly isolating, and it's understandable why you're questioning the point of it all. When the core of who you are feels absent, the motivation to keep going can vanish completely. It's a very real symptom of deep distress, and it suggests that the \"self\" you're trying to hold onto is simply exhausted. If you can't feel the point, maybe the most immediate point is finding a way to ease the weight of this emptiness, and that requires professional help.",
      "source": "target",
